1
00:00:06,975 --> 00:00:09,065
Last time, our plant was drooping.

2
00:00:09,295 --> 00:00:10,415
It was wilting.

3
00:00:10,655 --> 00:00:12,285
It did not have enough water.

4
00:00:12,515 --> 00:00:15,435
Our mealworm got a lid with holes, so air can get in.

5
00:00:15,665 --> 00:00:16,825
Now, room three.

6
00:00:17,065 --> 00:00:18,565
What is under Pip's cloth?

7
00:00:19,217 --> 00:00:23,017
Today you will learn why living things need food, how a plant

8
00:00:22,767 --> 00:00:25,757
gets its food, and the three needs of living things.

9
00:00:26,188 --> 00:00:27,368
Lock in first.

10
00:00:27,588 --> 00:00:29,008
And find the new lizard!

11
00:00:29,584 --> 00:00:30,624
First, food.

12
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:33,044
After PE, you feel hungry.

13
00:00:33,274 --> 00:00:35,074
You used up lots of energy.

14
00:00:35,314 --> 00:00:36,264
So you eat.

15
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:37,944
Our mealworm eats too.

16
00:00:38,823 --> 00:00:39,923
Say it with me!

17
00:00:40,636 --> 00:00:42,366
All living things need food.

18
00:00:42,596 --> 00:00:44,966
Food provides living things with energy.

19
00:00:51,364 --> 00:00:52,334
You eat rice.

20
00:00:52,524 --> 00:00:54,144
The mealworm eats oats.

21
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:55,884
But nobody feeds a plant.

22
00:00:55,914 --> 00:00:57,494
So who feeds a plant?

23
00:00:59,248 --> 00:01:01,648
Two weeks ago, I started a needs test.

24
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:03,218
Two bean plants.

25
00:01:03,448 --> 00:01:04,528
Same pot.

26
00:01:04,698 --> 00:01:05,758
Same soil.

27
00:01:06,048 --> 00:01:07,748
Same water every day.

28
00:01:07,938 --> 00:01:09,238
One by the window.

29
00:01:09,478 --> 00:01:11,068
One in a dark cupboard.

30
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:14,520
Round one.

31
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:16,400
The cupboard plant had water.

32
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,530
It had air.

33
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,380
So which need was it missing?

34
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:20,610
One, water.

35
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,750
Two, food.

36
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:22,980
Three, air.

37
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:24,630
Show me with your fingers.

38
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:31,046
Locked in!

39
00:01:31,176 --> 00:01:31,986
Three, air!

40
00:01:32,126 --> 00:01:33,526
The cupboard door was shut!

41
00:01:33,573 --> 00:01:34,593
Two, food!

42
00:01:34,683 --> 00:01:36,633
Nobody put food in its pot!

43
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,730
Two, food.

44
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:39,830
Only the light was different.

45
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,560
So the light must matter.

46
00:01:44,042 --> 00:01:45,322
The answer is two.

47
00:01:45,552 --> 00:01:46,332
Food.

48
00:01:46,552 --> 00:01:47,222
Look.

49
00:01:47,462 --> 00:01:49,642
The window plant is green and strong.

50
00:01:49,852 --> 00:01:51,872
The cupboard plant is pale and weak.

51
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:55,403
Basil, air still gets in around a cupboard door.

52
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,323
And Momo, two is right.

53
00:01:57,553 --> 00:01:58,343
But look.

54
00:01:58,583 --> 00:02:01,243
Nobody put food in the window plant's pot either.

55
00:02:01,306 --> 00:02:01,976
Oh!

56
00:02:02,106 --> 00:02:03,996
Then where does its food come from?

57
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:08,325
Say it with me!

58
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:12,173
Plants do not eat but they can make their own food when

59
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:12,843
there is light.

60
00:02:17,152 --> 00:02:20,072
In the dark cupboard, the plant could not make its food.

61
00:02:20,949 --> 00:02:22,259
Showed two fingers?

62
00:02:22,479 --> 00:02:24,369
One finger up on your score hand!

63
00:02:24,570 --> 00:02:26,060
Into the light you go.

64
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:27,830
I will keep watching.

65
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,450
My homework from last night.

66
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,910
Before the hotel!

67
00:02:33,036 --> 00:02:33,686
One.

68
00:02:33,826 --> 00:02:35,826
A bean plant is a living thing.

69
00:02:35,841 --> 00:02:36,631
Two.

70
00:02:36,661 --> 00:02:38,271
It needs water and air.

71
00:02:38,339 --> 00:02:38,925
Three.

72
00:02:38,735 --> 00:02:41,760
It does not need food because it does not eat.

73
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:43,084
Showdown!

74
00:02:43,324 --> 00:02:44,414
Double points.

75
00:02:44,644 --> 00:02:46,234
One line has a mistake.

76
00:02:46,454 --> 00:02:48,984
Is it line one, line two, or line three?

77
00:02:49,214 --> 00:02:50,614
Show me with your fingers.

78
00:02:57,089 --> 00:02:58,039
Locked in!

79
00:02:58,169 --> 00:02:58,979
Three.

80
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:01,089
All living things need food.

81
00:03:01,141 --> 00:03:01,871
Three!

82
00:03:01,961 --> 00:03:03,031
It does not eat.

83
00:03:03,051 --> 00:03:04,481
But it makes its own food.

84
00:03:04,641 --> 00:03:05,891
I learned that today!

85
00:03:05,939 --> 00:03:06,609
Oh!

86
00:03:06,739 --> 00:03:07,579
Three.

87
00:03:07,659 --> 00:03:09,039
I forgot food!

88
00:03:10,288 --> 00:03:10,948
Fixed!

89
00:03:11,178 --> 00:03:12,528
It needs food too.

90
00:03:12,658 --> 00:03:14,958
It makes its own food when there is light.

91
00:03:15,081 --> 00:03:16,341
Line two was true.

92
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,381
It just was not the whole list.

93
00:03:18,601 --> 00:03:19,921
Showed three fingers?

94
00:03:20,141 --> 00:03:22,021
Put up two more on your score hand!

95
00:03:22,968 --> 00:03:23,858
Sunset.

96
00:03:24,088 --> 00:03:25,028
Eight ticks.

97
00:03:25,248 --> 00:03:26,738
One box is empty.

98
00:03:26,978 --> 00:03:27,848
Room one.

99
00:03:28,098 --> 00:03:28,888
Food!

100
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:32,000
It stood by the window all day.

101
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,620
It made its own food!

102
00:03:33,899 --> 00:03:34,779
A plant.

103
00:03:35,029 --> 00:03:35,939
A mealworm.

104
00:03:36,189 --> 00:03:37,269
A bean plant.

105
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:38,829
Three different guests.

106
00:03:39,039 --> 00:03:40,479
The same three needs.

107
00:03:41,285 --> 00:03:42,495
Say it with me!

108
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:45,800
Living things need water, food and air.

109
00:03:47,724 --> 00:03:48,834
Say all three.

110
00:03:49,064 --> 00:03:50,074
Every time.

111
00:03:50,961 --> 00:03:52,021
Say it with us!

112
00:03:52,681 --> 00:03:53,371
Water!

113
00:03:53,093 --> 00:03:53,784
Food!

114
00:03:53,506 --> 00:03:54,196
Air!

115
00:03:55,981 --> 00:03:57,731
Living things need all three!

116
00:03:59,281 --> 00:03:59,971
Water!

117
00:03:59,693 --> 00:04:00,383
Food!

118
00:04:00,106 --> 00:04:00,796
Air!

119
00:04:00,931 --> 00:04:02,681
Living things need all three!

120
00:04:03,536 --> 00:04:04,926
Show me your score hand!

121
00:04:05,156 --> 00:04:06,166
More than two?

122
00:04:06,396 --> 00:04:07,676
You beat the Buddies.

123
00:04:07,896 --> 00:04:08,956
Three fingers?

124
00:04:09,176 --> 00:04:10,176
High five!

125
00:04:10,973 --> 00:04:12,333
Did you spot the lizard?

126
00:04:12,573 --> 00:04:14,733
It was behind the clock, at sunset.

127
00:04:14,953 --> 00:04:16,293
What does a lizard need?

128
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:17,813
Tell someone at home.

129
00:04:19,246 --> 00:04:20,436
Day thirty-two.

130
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:21,806
Check-out time.

131
00:04:22,046 --> 00:04:24,056
Our mealworm goes back to its tub.

132
00:04:26,059 --> 00:04:26,649
Whoa!

133
00:04:26,819 --> 00:04:28,849
I touched this plant and it folded up!

134
00:04:28,975 --> 00:04:30,895
Touch this plant and it folds up!

135
00:04:31,135 --> 00:04:32,245
What is it doing?

136
00:04:32,495 --> 00:04:34,365
Lock in your answer for next time.

137
00:04:35,399 --> 00:04:37,559
Let's read today's key words together!

138
00:04:37,799 --> 00:04:38,519
Ready?

139
00:04:38,809 --> 00:04:39,569
Food.

140
00:04:40,965 --> 00:04:41,775
Energy.

141
00:04:43,337 --> 00:04:43,934
Light.

142
00:04:45,351 --> 00:04:46,251
Well done!

143
00:04:47,234 --> 00:04:48,295
Say it with us!

144
00:04:49,095 --> 00:04:49,805
Ready?

145
00:04:49,929 --> 00:04:50,549
One!

146
00:04:50,929 --> 00:04:51,609
Two!

147
00:04:51,934 --> 00:04:53,109
Now you know!
